  <p class="gd-byline" style="font-family:var(--sans);font-size:12.5px;letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--blue-soft);opacity:.9;margin:16px 0 0">By <a href="/about" style="color:inherit;text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px">Heliski Travel Team</a> · Updated 11 Aug 2026</p>
  <p class="gd-lede">A question we hear often: am I too old for this? The honest answer, for the vast majority of skiers, is no. Heli-skiing has no upper age limit, and plenty of people ski their best-ever trips in their 50s, 60s and beyond. What matters is ability and fitness, not the number on your passport. This guide covers what really counts at this stage, how to prepare, and why Iceland suits older skiers so well, before you look at <a href="/packages">the packages</a>.</p>
